    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "Q1: How long does the entire licensing process take? ",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
     "@type": "Answer",
     "text": "The time to complete the process depends on your schedule and pace. On average, completing pre-licensing education, taking the exam, and submitting your application can take 4-6 weeks. "
    }
   },
   {
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "Q2: Can I take the licensing exam online? ",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
     "@type": "Answer",
     "text": "Yes, Georgia offers online proctoring for insurance exams, allowing you to take the test from home. Check with Pearson VUE to see if you meet the technical requirements. "
    }
   },
   {
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "Q3: What if I fail the exam? ",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
     "@type": "Answer",
     "text": "If you don’t pass, you can retake the exam. However, you’ll need to pay the exam fee again, so take advantage of study resources before retesting. "
    }
   },
   {
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "Q4: Is a college degree required to become an insurance agent in Georgia? ",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
     "@type": "Answer",
     "text": "No, a college degree is not necessary. However, completing the pre-licensing education and passing the exam are essential steps in the process. "
    }
   },
   {
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "Q5: Are there any residency requirements for obtaining a Georgia insurance license? ",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
     "@type": "Answer",
     "text": "Yes, you must be a Georgia resident or meet specific non-resident requirements to obtain a license in the state. "
    }
   }
